{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"froggy-brightish-xiphias","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\n`scripts/gerrit_safe_submit.py` reads the change, refuses a stale `--revision`, then checks the `LLM-Review` and `Verified` labels with `_label_ok`, which needs the label's `approved` summary. Gerrit omits `approved` on a closed change, so re-running the script on a change that already merged reports a vote problem instead of the merge.\n\nObserved 2026-11-13 against change 3393 (MERGED, submitted 2026-11-13 04:09 PST, both votes +1 in `labels.*.all`), read-only:\n- `--revision aa1681bb531e3a607c7366cde951e263b51ba78f` (the merged revision): `refusing submit: missing live labels=['LLM-Review', 'Verified'], unresolved=0, submittable=False`, exit 3.\n- `--revision 0000…0000`: `refusing stale submit: inspected 0000…, current is aa1681bb…`, exit 2; correct and safe, but it does not say the change is merged.\n\nThe script's own reconcile path (Gerrit 3393's parent change, `5a4efd52a39`) already treats \"merged at the submitted revision\" as success (exit 0, says so). The pre-submit path should report the same state the same way rather than send the operator after votes that exist.\n\n## Approach\nIn `main`, right after `read_change()` and before the stale and label checks, branch on `detail[\"status\"]`:\n- `MERGED` and `--revision` equals the merged `current_revision`: print `change <n> is already merged at <sha>; nothing to submit` and return 0.\n- `MERGED` at a different revision: print that it is merged at `<current>`, not at the inspected revision, and return 2 (the stale-revision code).\n- `ABANDONED`: print that and return 3.\nNo POST of any kind on these paths (no hashtag, no submit). Update the module docstring's exit-code list. No new flag, config key or env var.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A MERGED change with the matching revision exits 0, prints `already merged`, and sends no POST.\n- [ ] A MERGED change with a different revision exits 2 and names both SHAs and `MERGED`, with no POST.\n- [ ] An ABANDONED change exits 3 and says abandoned, with no POST.\n- [ ] Open-change behavior is unchanged; proved by `pytest tests/unit/test_gerrit_submit_if_current_8b1c.py`.\n\n## Testing\nAdd RED cases to `tests/unit/test_gerrit_submit_if_current_8b1c.py` using its existing fake Gerrit, asserting exit code, message and that no POST was recorded. Then run the file, `make verify`, and a read-only live run against change 3393 with `--hashtag \"\"`.","id":"1f9a-a161-bd35-404e","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"gerrit_safe_submit.py reports \"missing live labels\" for an already-merged change"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1794590362950282939,"uuid":"375d28fd-7e80-4a0b-b0d0-bc33720301c4"}